    "id": "4bd984c40e3e73843f5e86bcd560892e6c2f3fcc",
    "tree_id": "e37719f6bbe65586cf22063eb6aa84c9c3c47266",
    "distinct": true,
    "message": "Fix a CI-only race in the webhook log-record tests (#261)\n\nCI caught what this machine never did:\n\n    IndexError: list index out of range\n    r = _one_record(server, \"/webhook/github\")[0]\n\nFour call sites removed the log stream's handler in a `finally` immediately\nafter the client's `getresponse()` returned. The request is handled on a\nbackground thread that logs *after* it writes the response -- the client\nreceiving the bytes is no guarantee that thread has reached the log call yet.\nRemoving the handler before it does is worse than reading too early: a log\ncall reaching a logger with no handler attached goes nowhere, so the record\nis discarded outright, not just missed on this read.\n\nThis machine is fast enough that the race never lost. CI, evidently, is not.\n\nConsolidated the four duplicated try/finally blocks into one `_capture()`\nhelper that waits for at least one record before tearing the handler down --\nthe same deadline-poll pattern `test_logs.py` already uses elsewhere in this\nsuite for the identical reason. Verified with five repeated local runs and\nthe full gate: 723 bus tests, 213 cloud tests, 0 type errors.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zWFQQKgFbvcNASW6nXwTR\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-03T16:30:14+01:00",
